diff --git a/doc/source/reference/compute/kerbside-guide.rst b/doc/source/reference/compute/kerbside-guide.rst
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..26573a40b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/source/reference/compute/kerbside-guide.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@
+.. _kerbside-guide:
+
+==========================
+Kerbside - SPICE VDI proxy
+==========================
+
+Overview
+~~~~~~~~
+
+`Kerbside <https://github.com/shakenfist/kerbside>`__ is a SPICE protocol
+proxy which provides VDI access to virtual machines running inside an
+OpenStack cloud. Unlike layer 4 proxies which pass through unparsed traffic,
+Kerbside understands the SPICE protocol itself -- it terminates TLS, drives
+the SPICE link handshake, and acts as an enforcing SPICE application
+firewall. This allows users to be offered rich native SPICE desktop sessions
+(high resolution, multiple monitors, USB passthrough and audio) instead of
+HTML5-transcoded consoles.
+
+Kolla Ansible deploys the Kerbside REST API (``kerbside_api``) and SPICE
+proxy (``kerbside_proxy``) containers when ``enable_kerbside`` is set in
+``/etc/kolla/globals.yml``. Kerbside proxies Nova SPICE consoles, so
+``nova_console`` must also be set to ``spice``. The Kerbside prechecks fail
+if it is not:
+
+.. code-block:: yaml
+
+   enable_kerbside: "yes"
+   nova_console: "spice"
+
+A dedicated Keystone user (``kerbside`` by default, named by
+``kerbside_keystone_user``) is registered during deployment. Kerbside uses
+this user to look up console details via the Nova API, which it reaches on
+the internal endpoint unless ``kerbside_nova_interface`` says otherwise.
+
+Connecting to consoles
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Users connect to a console by fetching a ``.vv`` file describing the session
+from the Kerbside API and passing it to a native SPICE client such as
+``remote-viewer``. Nova advertises the URL these files are fetched from,
+which defaults to the external VIP but may be overridden in
+``/etc/kolla/globals.yml``:
+
+.. code-block:: yaml
+
+   kerbside_spice_direct_proxy_base_url: >-
+     https://vdi.example.com:13002/nova-console.vv
+
+SPICE sessions between clients and the proxy are always secured with TLS,
+and the CA certificate in use is included in the ``.vv`` files served to
+users. For test deployments these certificates can be generated by the
+``kolla-ansible certificates`` command, which generates certificates for
+Kerbside when ``certificates_generate_kerbside`` is enabled. That variable
+defaults to the value of ``enable_kerbside``.
+
+Upgrades
+~~~~~~~~
+
+Kerbside does not support running its processes against differing database
+schema versions, so ``kolla-ansible upgrade`` stops every ``kerbside_api``
+and ``kerbside_proxy`` container across the deployment before migrating the
+database, and starts them again on the new images once the migration has
+completed. There is therefore no rolling upgrade path for Kerbside, and an
+upgrade interrupts any SPICE console sessions which are in flight at the
+time. Clients must reconnect once the upgrade has finished, which requires
+fetching a new ``.vv`` file.
+
+.. warning::
+
+   Staged upgrades using ``kolla_serial`` are not supported for Kerbside.
+   Upgrading the deployment in batches leaves the hosts in the later batches
+   running the previous version of Kerbside against a database which has
+   already been migrated, which is not a supported configuration.
